    }
  ],
  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "m17-s001",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-a",
      "startMs": 0,
      "endMs": 5540,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thanks all. Nadia ran the usability sessions this week, so over to her."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s002",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-c",
      "startMs": 5790,
      "endMs": 13990,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "We tested with five front-desk staff across two clinics. Four of the five completed a full intake without any help."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s003",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-b",
      "startMs": 14240,
      "endMs": 16740,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "That's better than I expected."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s004",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-c",
      "startMs": 16990,
      "endMs": 23290,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "The one who struggled got stuck on the medication search. The list was too long."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s005",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-d",
      "startMs": 23540,
      "endMs": 30220,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Medication is where accuracy matters most, so I'd rather we fix that than simplify it away."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s006",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-c",
      "startMs": 30470,
      "endMs": 34870,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Agreed. I'm thinking type-ahead with the most common medications first."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s007",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-a",
      "startMs": 35120,
      "endMs": 40280,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "We also tested the two layouts. Single page versus the step-by-step wizard."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s008",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-c",
      "startMs": 40530,
      "endMs": 47210,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Single page won clearly. Staff could see everything at once and jump back to fix mistakes."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s009",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-b",
      "startMs": 47460,
      "endMs": 50720,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Then we keep the single-page form. Decided."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s010",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-d",
      "startMs": 50970,
      "endMs": 55750,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Fine by me, as long as allergies stay at the top."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s011",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-c",
      "startMs": 56000,
      "endMs": 57360,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "They will."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s012",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-a",
      "startMs": 57610,
      "endMs": 61250,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "What's left before we can hand over designs?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s013",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-c",
      "startMs": 61500,
      "endMs": 68940,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "The medication search, the high contrast theme, and error states. I'll ship the final designs by May 15."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s014",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-b",
      "startMs": 69190,
      "endMs": 73590,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'd like to see them before they go to engineering."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s015",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-c",
      "startMs": 73840,
      "endMs": 77480,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Of course, I'll send them to you first."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s016",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-a",
      "startMs": 77730,
      "endMs": 80610,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Samir, anything from the clinical side?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s017",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-d",
      "startMs": 80860,
      "endMs": 89820,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "The wording on the consent step needs clinical review. I'll review the consent wording and send changes to Nadia by next Friday."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s018",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-c",
      "startMs": 90070,
      "endMs": 91050,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s019",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-b",
      "startMs": 91300,
      "endMs": 97600,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "One organisational thing, I'm the product owner for this but Samir signs off anything clinical."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s020",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-a",
      "startMs": 97850,
      "endMs": 99590,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Understood, two sign-offs."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s021",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-d",
      "startMs": 99840,
      "endMs": 101200,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "That's right."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17-s022",
      "speakerId": "m17-spk-a",
      "startMs": 101450,
      "endMs": 107370,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Great. So: single page, final designs by May 15, consent wording by next Friday."
    }
  ],
  "note": {
    "version": 1,
    "body": "# Corvid usability test debrief\n\n**Date:** April 30\n**Attendees:** Alex Rivera (Larkspur Labs), Nadia Brooks (Larkspur Labs), Elif Kaya (Corvid Health), Samir Haddad (Corvid Health)\n\n## Summary\n\nDebrief of the first usability round on the Corvid Health patient intake redesign. Nadia ran the sessions this week with five front-desk staff across two clinics.\n\n## Results\n\n- Four of the five testers completed a full intake without any help.\n- The one who struggled got stuck on the medication search; the list was too long.\n- Samir wants the medication step fixed rather than simplified, because medication is where accuracy matters most. Nadia proposed type-ahead with the most common medications first.\n- The single-page layout clearly beat the step-by-step wizard: staff could see everything at once and jump back to fix mistakes.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- **Keep the single-page form**, with allergies at the top.\n- Two sign-offs apply: Elif as product owner, and Samir for anything clinical.\n\n## Action items\n\n- **Nadia Brooks** — ship the final designs (medication search, high contrast theme, error states) by May 15, sending them to Elif before engineering.\n- **Samir Haddad** — review the consent step wording and send changes to Nadia by next Friday.\n\n## Next steps\n\nOnce designs are signed off, engineering picks up the build for the first walk-in clinic.\n"
  },
